The prompt’s contract is the unbounded positive-index version of the prime-Fibonacci sequence. I’m using a straightforward implementation that generates Fibonacci numbers and checks each candidate by trial division; this keeps both the Python behavior and the K semantics small enough to audit, while avoiding any finite lookup table.
